{#
  FAQPage JSON-LD — layout-level, single-sourced from the `faq` front-matter
  array (the SAME array components/page-faq.njk renders visibly). Emitted once
  from base.njk's <head>. Renders nothing when `faq` is absent.

  Single-source rationale: Google policy requires the schema to match the
  visible text exactly; the old pattern kept two hand-synced copies (visible
  block + JSON-LD in the -head.html file) with a silent drift footgun. Here both
  representations read the one `faq` array, so they cannot drift.

  Escaping: `| dump` is JSON.stringify — it produces valid JSON strings for the
  em-dashes, curly apostrophes and quotes the answers contain (a hand-rolled
  concat would not). `faqStripTags` reduces an answer that carries an inline
  link to the plain text that matches the visible block's textContent (schema
  answer text is safest as plain text). See STYLE_GUIDE §6.40.
#}
{%- if faq and faq.length > 0 -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
{%- for item in faq %}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ item.q | faqStripTags | dump | safe }},
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | faqStripTags | dump | safe }} }
    }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}
